# Cloudflare Pages — SPA routing for the two entries.
#
# /admin/* → serve the admin SPA's index.html (admin handles its own
#            hash routing internally for #pr / #vs / #shop / etc.)
# /*       → serve the public SPA's index.html (router in main.js
#            maps the path to a tab — /news, /pr, /vssound, /shop,
#            /tools, /about, /news/{id} for individual articles)
#
# Order matters: Cloudflare evaluates top→bottom and stops at the
# first match. /admin must be listed before /* so admin URLs don't
# fall through to the public SPA.

# /passport/* → SAMO Passport lives in a SEPARATE repo (samomdkkupassport) and
#              is served by nginx from /var/www/passport/ on the VM. A
#              Cloudflare preview builds only THIS repo, so the path does not
#              exist here — and the catch-all below answered it 200 with the
#              PUBLIC APP'S OWN HTML, so the Passport button opened a new tab
#              showing the same site again, with no error anywhere. Reported
#              2026-08-31. A catch-all makes every missing path look like a
#              working one; this names the one we KNOW is missing.
#              ⚠️ Cloudflare only — nginx never reads this file and keeps
#              serving /passport/ from its own location block. Production is
#              untouched.

/admin/*     /admin/index.html          200
/passport/*  /passport-elsewhere.html   200
/passport    /passport-elsewhere.html   200
/*           /index.html                200
